  "statement": "On the ellipse $x^2+[$a]y^2=[$a]$, find $y''$ at $(0,1)$.\n\n[__________]{a}",
  "hints": [
    "Differentiate once to get $x+ayy'=0$.",
    "The first derivative is zero at $(0,1)$.",
    "Differentiate that equation using the product rule again."
  ],
  "solution": "$1+[$a](y')^2+[$a]yy''=0$. At $(0,1)$, this gives $y''=-1/[$a]$.",
